The goto rollback chain is the core challenge. Each label undoes exactly one
registration and falls through to the next. The labels run in reverse order of
the registrations. Draw the chain on paper first.

The exit function is the mirror image: unregister in exact reverse order of
init. If you registered mkdir, getdents, read, tcp4, tcp6, then exit
unregisters tcp6, tcp4, read, getdents, mkdir.

For the command dispatcher, use a chain of strncmp calls. Handle the exact
matches first (e, cloak, uncloak, persist, unpersist), then the prefix matches
(h.f., u.f., h.i., u.i., h.c., u.c., h.p., u.p., p.). Return -ENOENT for
anything unrecognized.
